SEC 7.  THE MERGE.  z_ij >= -(1/n + x_i + y_j) on the collar, so
    every ODD one-sided step degrades: p_m(z) >= -sum_ij d_ij^{m-2}
    z_ij^2 with d_ij = 1/n + x_i + y_j.  Both signs of p_m are tested;
    a lower bound tested only where the quantity is positive proves
    nothing.
    n=6 k=4: entry True  step True  binomial True  eta True   points 5   with p_3 < 0: 2
    n=8 k=5: entry True  step True  binomial True  eta True   points 5   with p_3 < 0: 4
    n=10 k=5: entry True  step True  binomial True  eta True   points 5   with p_3 < 0: 4
    n=12 k=6: entry True  step True  binomial True  eta True   points 5   with p_3 < 0: 3
    Xi_a = sum_{u+v=a} C(a,u) D_{u,v} and D_{u,v} is the DOUBLE-EDGE
    atom, whose coefficient inside Theta_2[u,v] is (u+1)(v+1)/2:
    dbl_coef = (u+1)(v+1)/2 and Theta_2[1,0] = D_{1,0}: True

